{"name":"Cultist Robe","hex":"#331233","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cultist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of a cult."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cultist"},{"term":"robe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long loose outer garment, often signifying honorary stature.","The skin of an animal, especially the bison, dressed with the fur on, and used as a wrap."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To clothe; to dress.","To put on official vestments."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/robe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cult","blocks":[{"text":"Cults are social groups which have unusual, and often extreme, religious, spiritual or philosophical beliefs and rituals. Extreme devotion to a particular person, object, or goal is another characteristic often ascribed to cults. The term has different, divergent and often pejorative definitions both in popular culture and academia and has been an ongoing source of contention among scholars across several fields of study."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cult"},{"title":"Robe","blocks":[{"text":"A robe is a loose-fitting outer garment. Unlike garments described as capes or cloaks, robes usually have sleeves. The English word robe derives from Middle English robe (\"garment\"), borrowed from Old French robe, itself taken from the Frankish word *rouba, and is related to the word rob."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/LongPao.JPG/330px-LongPao.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robe"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Max_Weber_1894.jpg/330px-Max_Weber_1894.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Max_Weber_1894.jpg/330px-Max_Weber_1894.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=p